Promise that resolves after httpServer.close() and wss.close() complete (wrap
their callback-style closes in Promises and await both), then make the shutdown
handler async (function shutdown() { ... }) and await server.stop() before
calling process.exit(0) (i.e., await server.stop(); process.exit(0)); update any
call sites accordingly so graceful shutdown waits for HTTP and WebSocket cleanup
to finish.
```

